{
  "schema": "rosw-brushes-patch-cases/1",
  "about": "Patches and the PatchReport each must give (docs/CONTRACTS.md F3, Patches). Python is the authority (brush_model.apply_patch, run by tests/test_brush_model.py); the app runs the same cases against its own advisory check. Authored by hand; no script writes this file.",
  "base": "A case runs against a brush made of the schema alone: every key of eras[era].key_order in silica_keys.json with its row's `default` (a curve also takes the `resolution` its class gives the era's family: 1024 for legacy, none for modern), then each key of `assign` set to the value given, in the forms of F3 (a key the schema does not list goes last in the key order). This is brush_model.case_base(era, assign). It is a test base, not a brush the app wrote and not the new-brush template.",
  "run": "apply_patch(base, changes, mode=mode, allow_unknown=allow_unknown). `mode` is \"strict\" and `allow_unknown` false where a case does not say.",
  "compare": "`ok`, `era`, `applied`, `clamped`, `unchanged` and `warnings` are compared whole, as JSON values. `rejected` is compared item by item, in order, on `key`, `code` and `value`; `reason` is prose for a person and is not compared.",
  "cases": [
    {
      "id": "real-takes-a-whole-number",
      "about": "A JSON whole number on a real key is the real 1.0.",
      "era": "M220",
      "changes": {
        "plotSpacing": 1
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "era": "M220",
        "applied": {
          "plotSpacing": 1.0
        },
        "clamped": [],
        "rejected": [],
        "unchanged": [],
        "warnings": []
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "real-is-rounded-to-32-bits",
      "about": "0.1 is stored as the nearest 32-bit float, widened.",
      "era": "M220",
      "changes": {
        "plotSpacing": 0.1
      },
      "expect": {
        "ok": true,
        "era": "M220",
        "applied": {
          "plotSpacing": 0.10000000149011612
        },
        "clamped": [],
        "rejected": [],
        "unchanged": [],
        "warnings": []
      }
    },
